    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0268" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/10–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-30T20:00:00-05:00">October 30, 1946—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1403. Unless you perceive some reason for not doing so please seek occasion to
                    make it clear that although this Govt would of course welcome visit by Tsaldaris
                    to US it feels it would be unfortunate for him leave Greece this critical time
                    in order present the national claims at CFM. It
                    seems to us task of broadening govt and endeavoring to strengthen Greece
                    internally is most important one that can face a Greek PriMin at present time.</p>
                <p>Brit Emb has informed Dept that similar UK views have been expressed to Greeks by
                    your Brit colleague.</p>
                <p>Sent Athens; rptd London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
